WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.307
Now we can put several ideas together into one complete workflow.

00:00:04.307 --> 00:00:07.462
We begin with the raw orders DataFrame.

00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:11.817
First, we convert the date column to a real datetime value.

00:00:11.817 --> 00:00:14.997
Then we keep valid positive amounts.

00:00:14.997 --> 00:00:22.822
Next, we create a monthly period, group by month and region, calculate total sales and order counts,

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.839
and finally sort the results.

00:00:25.545 --> 00:00:29.352
This is closer to what Pandas work looks like in a real project.

00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:33.657
One function rarely solves the whole problem.

00:00:33.657 --> 00:00:39.812
Instead, we build a sequence of small transformations, with each step answering a specific question.

00:00:39.812 --> 00:00:47.297
Before running the code, read the chain from top to bottom and explain what each line is doing in plain language.

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:50.582
Then run it and inspect the final report.

00:00:50.582 --> 00:00:57.717
If you can understand how the raw rows became the final summary, you are thinking about Pandas as a workflow rather than

00:00:57.717 --> 00:01:00.656
as a collection of unrelated commands.
